---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Pursuit of AGI Resolves the Three-Body Problem in Computing"
  description="About: The Pursuit of AGI Resolves the Three-Body Problem in Computing. Research paper in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      The Pursuit of AGI Resolves the Three-Body Problem in Computing
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Computing has three bodies: the theorists who state what a system should do, the makers who build it, and the users who run it. Each body is coherent on its own. The instability lives in the interfaces between them, where each side assumes the handoff is absent or belongs to someone else, so the assumption is never written down or checked.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The paper borrows the three-body problem of celestial mechanics with care. Poincaré showed why no useful general formula exists, and Lagrange found the special configurations that stay stable in a frame moving with the bodies. The paper keeps analogy and mechanism apart, and states the interface thesis as definitions, five propositions, protocols and falsifiers.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      A system that aims at general intelligence must act across all three bodies and every level of the stack, so it cannot leave any interface assumption implicit. Pursued seriously, that aim forces every assumption to be made explicit and checked. In a stack built that way, a correction stays where it is made and carries upward. The Reality Code Engine's whole-stack interface checks are the first evidence.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-papers">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion papers</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Research papers: <a href="/papers/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Reality Code Engine</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/agency/" class="text-brand-cyan">Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/gates/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metered Commit Gates</a>.
        Economics companion: <a href="/papers/interface-economics/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Price of the Unexamined Interface</a> · <a href="/papers/ai-coding-market/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Promised Trillion Dollar AI-Coding Market</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/three-body/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/three-body/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/three-body.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
